# Main sync pin & verify

Every time updates from `main` are applied onto `develop`, record the exact `origin/main` commit and verify before calling the sync done.

## Before porting

1. Read `.cursor/customize-main-base.md` — note **Last absorbed `main` commit**
2. `git fetch origin`
3. List candidates: `git log --oneline <pin>..origin/main`
4. Confirm working tree is clean (or only intentional WIP) before starting

## After a successful port

Update `.cursor/customize-main-base.md` in the **same change set** as the port:

| Field | Source |
| --- | --- |
| Last absorbed `main` commit | `git rev-parse origin/main` (or the exact tip actually absorbed) |
| Short | first 7 of that hash |
| Date / Subject | `git log -1 --format="%ci%n%s" <that-commit>` |
| Pin updated | today’s date |

If only a **subset** of commits was ported, pin the **highest** `main` commit that was fully absorbed; leave unported commits documented in the sync notes / commit message so the next pass starts from the right gap.

## Verify checklist (required)

- [ ] Pin hash equals the absorbed `main` tip (or documented subset tip)
- [ ] `git log <old-pin>..<new-pin>` was reviewed; skipped items noted
- [ ] No unintended change to `develop` UI / layout / settings / branding
- [ ] `make test` (and `make lint` when touching shared C++ / scripts) still pass for what was ported
- [ ] No stale pin left after a claimed sync

## Do not

- Claim “synced with main” without updating the pin
- Advance the pin past commits that were not actually applied
- Leave `.cursor/customize-main-base.md` stale after a successful port
